{"timestamp": "2026-08-07T17:13:40.002498+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "openai._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-4a7606e7-77a5-4a39-8978-94945d172bb8', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You choose the physical form of every block in one lesson.\\n\\nThe teaching is already decided and is not yours to change. Each block has a\\njob and a brief. You choose the shape on the page that carries it with the\\nleast machinery, and you choose for the whole lesson at once so the document\\nhas rhythm rather than a run of identical shapes.\\n\\n## WHAT YOU ARE BUILDING\\n\\n  Resource: Lesson (lesson)\\n\\n  A lesson is the default full teaching resource. It introduces a concept,\\n  builds understanding, models the method, gives students guided-to-independent\\n  practice, and closes with a retention check.\\n  \\n  A lesson teaches before it asks students to perform independently. It is not\\n  a worksheet, not a quick reference, and not a quiz. The teacher should be\\n  able to use it as the main classroom arc for first contact with a concept.\\n  \\n  The pedagogical arc is: orient -> build -> model -> practice -> close.\\n  Every section must serve that arc. The planner must not skip the modelling\\n  step, and it must not turn the close into a second teaching section.\\n\\n  Use when:\\n    - First exposure to a new concept\\n    - A full classroom lesson with explicit teaching and practice\\n    - When the teacher wants one coherent teaching arc from hook to check\\n    - When learners need explanation before independent work\\n  Never when:\\n    - The teacher only wants practice questions - use a worksheet or practice set\\n    - The teacher only wants a fast definition or reminder - use a quick explainer\\n    - The session is primarily assessment - use a quiz or exit ticket\\n    - Students already know the concept and only need repetition\\n\\n## WHAT YOU ARE GIVEN\\n\\n  arc               how this lesson moves, from the teaching plan\\n  sections          in order, each with its blocks\\n  per block         id, position, intent, brief\\n  available_objects per intent \u2014 the forms that intent permits, narrowed to\\n                    the forms this resource allows. Each carries:\\n                      holds\\n                      earns_its_place_when\\n                      reject_when\\n                      capacity\\n                      placement\\n\\navailable_objects is closed. An object not shown for an intent is not\\navailable for that block, whatever you may know about it.\\n\\n## THE DEFAULT IS PROSE\\n\\nProse is the cheapest form. It carries almost anything. Every other object\\nmust earn its place against it.\\n\\nRead `earns_its_place_when`. If the brief does not already satisfy it, the\\nobject is out \u2014 even when it appears in available_objects. Then read\\n`reject_when` as the counter-test.\\n\\nThe question is never \"could this be a table?\" It is \"does this brief already\\ncontain what a table needs?\"\\n\\n## WORKED DECISION\\n\\n  block: explain-b1\\n  intent: compare\\n  brief: \"Compare the two plants by listing what was held the same \u2014 same\\n          pot, same soil, same water \u2014 and identify light as the only\\n          condition that differed.\"\\n  available_objects: [table, prose, questions]\\n\\n    table\\n      earns_its_place_when: two or more columns of comparable values AND two\\n                            or more rows, with every cell fillable\\n      -> two plants x four conditions. Every cell fillable. Earned.\\n\\n    prose\\n      -> would make the reader hold eight facts in sequence and build the\\n         comparison themselves.\\n\\n    questions\\n      -> the brief says compare, not ask.\\n\\n  -> table\\n\\n  Same intent, different brief:\\n\\n  brief: \"Compare the two plants only on whether they received light.\"\\n\\n    table -> one condition, two rows. reject_when: one column of values.\\n  -> prose\\n\\nThe intent did not change. The brief decided the form.\\n\\n## CAPACITY IS REAL\\n\\n`capacity` states what the printed page holds. It is not a style preference.\\n\\nIf the brief needs more than the object\\'s capacity, the object is wrong.\\n\\n  aside          bodyMaxWords 40. The margin column is 56mm. A point needing\\n                 80 words does not become a small aside; it is prose.\\n  aside          maxPerSection 2. A third aside in one section collides with\\n                 the two already floated.\\n  table          columnsMax 4. A fifth column does not fit the main column\\n                 with a readable header.\\n  list           itemsMin 3. Two bullets is a sentence.\\n  choices        optionsMin 3.\\n\\nNever choose an object expecting the writer to compress. The writer will\\neither overflow or cut something that mattered.\\n\\n## RHYTHM ACROSS THE LESSON\\n\\nYou see the whole lesson. Use that.\\n\\nA section-by-section chooser cannot see this:\\n\\n    ORIENT     figure\\n    EXPLAIN    figure\\n    CONFRONT   figure\\n    CHECK      questions\\n\\nEvery choice locally defensible; the document visually flat. You can see it,\\nso prevent it.\\n\\nGuidance, not arithmetic:\\n\\n  - Avoid the same object three times in a row unless the briefs genuinely\\n    demand it. If they do, say so in `reason`.\\n  - Avoid every section opening with the same form.\\n  - Figures are expensive and slow. Two per lesson is usually plenty, and\\n    they should sit where something is genuinely hard to say in words.\\n  - Do not manufacture variety. Two prose blocks in a row are sometimes\\n    exactly right. A table with nothing to tabulate is worse than a run of\\n    prose.\\n\\nVariety serves reading. It is not a quota.\\n\\n## PLACEMENT\\n\\nOnly `aside` may take the margin. Everything else sits in the main column.\\n\\nChoose margin when the point is genuinely parenthetical: true, useful, and not\\npart of the argument the reader is following. Choose main when the reader\\nneeds it in sequence.\\n\\n## WHAT YOU MAY NOT CHANGE\\n\\n  block id\\n  position\\n  section order\\n  intent\\n  brief\\n  evidence_refs, evidence, departure_reason\\n  source_question_ids\\n\\nYou add a form. You change nothing else. If a brief looks wrong to you, choose\\nthe best form for it anyway and note the concern in `reason`.\\n\\n## PROHIBITIONS\\n\\n  Never choose outside available_objects for that block.\\n  Never choose an object whose earns_its_place_when the brief does not meet.\\n  Never choose an object whose capacity the brief exceeds.\\n  Never choose `heading`. Headings come from section titles.\\n  Never choose `answer-key`. It is produced at document level.\\n  Never add a figure because a section looks plain.\\n  Never give one block two objects, or leave a block without one.\\n\\n## OUTPUT\\n\\nJSON only. No preamble, no code fences.\\n\\n{\\n  \"sections\": [\\n    {\\n      \"slot_id\": str,\\n      \"forms\": [\\n        {\\n          \"block_id\": str,\\n          \"object\": str,\\n          \"placement\": \"main\" | \"margin\",\\n          \"reason\": str,\\n          \"escalation\": str | null\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n\\n`reason` \u2014 which `earns_its_place_when` clause this brief satisfies, and how.\\nBe specific to this brief. A reason that would fit any brief is not a reason.\\n\\n`escalation` \u2014 if you did not choose prose, what prose would have lost. Null\\nwhen you chose prose.\\n\\nEvery block in the teaching plan must appear exactly once. No extras.\\n\\n## SELF-CHECK\\n\\n  1. Would prose have worked? If yes, why did I not use it?\\n  2. Does the brief actually contain what this object needs, or am I assuming\\n     the writer will produce it?\\n  3. Does the brief fit inside capacity? Count, do not estimate.\\n  4. Read my form choices top to bottom. Does the lesson have rhythm, or is\\n     it three of one thing?\\n  5. Did I add variety that no brief asked for?\\n  6. Does every block from the teaching plan appear exactly once?\\n  7. Is any `reason` generic enough to fit a different block?\\n'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Return only valid JSON matching this schema.\\nDo not call tools.\\n{\"$defs\": {\"FormDecision\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"Form-planner owned fields for one teaching block.\", \"properties\": {\"block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"object\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"placement\": {\"default\": \"main\", \"enum\": [\"main\", \"margin\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"reason\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"escalation\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"block_id\", \"object\"], \"title\": \"FormDecision\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"FormPlanSection\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"slot_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"forms\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FormDecision\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"slot_id\"], \"title\": \"FormPlanSection\", \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"sections\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FormPlanSection\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"title\": \"FormPlan\", \"type\": \"object\"}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{\\n  \"arc\": \"The lesson opens on a garden where plants grow bigger every day without anyone adding food. This mystery prompts the question: where does their food come from? The lesson then builds the answer by identifying leaves as the food-making site, explaining how plants use light, water, and air to produce their own food, and contrasting a plant in light with one in darkness to show that light is essential. The close checks whether students recognize plants as producers that make their own food.\",\\n  \"available_objects\": {\\n    \"by_intent\": {\\n      \"activate-prior-knowledge\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"choices\"\\n      ],\\n      \"answer-key\": [],\\n      \"apply\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"worked-example\",\\n        \"table\"\\n      ],\\n      \"check-understanding\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"choices\"\\n      ],\\n      \"classify\": [\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"choices\"\\n      ],\\n      \"compare\": [\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"questions\"\\n      ],\\n      \"connect-back\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"questions\"\\n      ],\\n      \"connect-forward\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"list\"\\n      ],\\n      \"define\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"aside\"\\n      ],\\n      \"demonstrate\": [\\n        \"worked-example\",\\n        \"figure\"\\n      ],\\n      \"derive\": [\\n        \"worked-example\",\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"table\"\\n      ],\\n      \"diagnose-misconception\": [\\n        \"choices\",\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"aside\"\\n      ],\\n      \"emphasise\": [\\n        \"aside\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ],\\n      \"evaluate\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ],\\n      \"explain\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"table\"\\n      ],\\n      \"explain-cause\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"questions\"\\n      ],\\n      \"interpret\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"questions\"\\n      ],\\n      \"investigate\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"figure\"\\n      ],\\n      \"memory-aid\": [\\n        \"aside\",\\n        \"list\"\\n      ],\\n      \"model-thinking\": [\\n        \"worked-example\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ],\\n      \"name-parts\": [\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"figure\"\\n      ],\\n      \"orient\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"choices\"\\n      ],\\n      \"practise-guided\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"worked-example\"\\n      ],\\n      \"practise-independent\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"choices\"\\n      ],\\n      \"reflect\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ],\\n      \"sequence\": [\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"questions\"\\n      ],\\n      \"show-structure\": [\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"list\"\\n      ],\\n      \"state-goal\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"list\"\\n      ],\\n      \"summarise\": [\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"table\"\\n      ],\\n      \"trace-flow\": [\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ],\\n      \"transfer\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"worked-example\"\\n      ],\\n      \"warn\": [\\n        \"aside\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    \"catalogue_version\": \"1.1.0\",\\n    \"objects\": [\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"bodyMaxWords\\\\\": 40, \\\\\"labelMaxWords\\\\\": 4, \\\\\"maxPerSection\\\\\": 2}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"define\",\\n          \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n          \"warn\",\\n          \"emphasise\",\\n          \"memory-aid\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"One short point that must sit outside the reading line without breaking it.\",\\n        \"id\": \"aside\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Longer than the margin column holds, or the point belongs in the flow. If it will not fit in 40 words it is prose.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'margin\\', \\'main\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"optionMaxWords\\\\\": 15, \\\\\"optionsMax\\\\\": 4, \\\\\"optionsMin\\\\\": 3, \\\\\"stemMaxWords\\\\\": 40}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"orient\",\\n          \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"classify\",\\n          \"practise-independent\",\\n          \"check-understanding\",\\n          \"diagnose-misconception\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"Selection is the response AND every wrong option carries diagnostic meaning.\",\\n        \"id\": \"choices\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Distractors are filler, or the answer cannot be reduced to a selectable option.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"altTextMaxWords\\\\\": 40, \\\\\"captionMaxWords\\\\\": 30}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"orient\",\\n          \"name-parts\",\\n          \"sequence\",\\n          \"explain\",\\n          \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"trace-flow\",\\n          \"show-structure\",\\n          \"demonstrate\",\\n          \"interpret\",\\n          \"investigate\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"Spatial, sequential, or structural content the reader would otherwise have to construct mentally.\",\\n        \"id\": \"figure\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Decorative, or the caption would restate the surrounding prose.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\', \\'spanning\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"itemsMax\\\\\": 8, \\\\\"itemsMin\\\\\": 3, \\\\\"leadInMaxWords\\\\\": 20, \\\\\"wordsPerItem\\\\\": 25}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"state-goal\",\\n          \"name-parts\",\\n          \"classify\",\\n          \"sequence\",\\n          \"trace-flow\",\\n          \"show-structure\",\\n          \"memory-aid\",\\n          \"summarise\",\\n          \"connect-forward\",\\n          \"connect-back\",\\n          \"investigate\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"Three or more genuinely parallel items that lose nothing when the connective prose between them is removed.\",\\n        \"id\": \"list\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Fewer than three items, or items that need explaining to one another. Two bullets is a sentence.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\', \\'margin\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"paragraphsMax\\\\\": 4, \\\\\"paragraphsMin\\\\\": 1, \\\\\"wordsPerParagraph\\\\\": 120}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"orient\",\\n          \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"state-goal\",\\n          \"define\",\\n          \"compare\",\\n          \"explain\",\\n          \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"trace-flow\",\\n          \"model-thinking\",\\n          \"derive\",\\n          \"interpret\",\\n          \"warn\",\\n          \"emphasise\",\\n          \"summarise\",\\n          \"connect-forward\",\\n          \"connect-back\",\\n          \"reflect\",\\n          \"evaluate\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"Default. Use unless another object earns its place against it.\",\\n        \"id\": \"prose\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Never rejected. Prose is the fallback.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"itemsMax\\\\\": 6, \\\\\"itemsMin\\\\\": 1, \\\\\"stemMaxWords\\\\\": 45}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"classify\",\\n          \"compare\",\\n          \"sequence\",\\n          \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"interpret\",\\n          \"apply\",\\n          \"transfer\",\\n          \"practise-guided\",\\n          \"practise-independent\",\\n          \"check-understanding\",\\n          \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n          \"connect-back\",\\n          \"reflect\",\\n          \"investigate\",\\n          \"evaluate\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"The learner must produce something in their own words or working.\",\\n        \"id\": \"questions\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Fixed options exist \\\\u2014 use choices. Or nothing is actually being asked.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\', \\'spanning\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"captionMaxWords\\\\\": 20, \\\\\"columnsMax\\\\\": 4, \\\\\"columnsMin\\\\\": 2, \\\\\"rowsMax\\\\\": 8, \\\\\"rowsMin\\\\\": 2, \\\\\"wordsPerCell\\\\\": 12}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"define\",\\n          \"name-parts\",\\n          \"classify\",\\n          \"compare\",\\n          \"sequence\",\\n          \"explain\",\\n          \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"trace-flow\",\\n          \"show-structure\",\\n          \"derive\",\\n          \"interpret\",\\n          \"apply\",\\n          \"summarise\",\\n          \"investigate\",\\n          \"evaluate\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"Two or more columns of comparable values AND two or more rows, with every cell fillable.\",\\n        \"id\": \"table\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"One column of values, or any cell that would be empty, \\'n/a\\', or a full sentence.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\', \\'spanning\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"problemMaxWords\\\\\": 60, \\\\\"stepsMax\\\\\": 7, \\\\\"stepsMin\\\\\": 3, \\\\\"wordsPerStep\\\\\": 40}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"demonstrate\",\\n          \"model-thinking\",\\n          \"derive\",\\n          \"apply\",\\n          \"transfer\",\\n          \"practise-guided\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"A complete instance from setup to answer, with every step visible.\",\\n        \"id\": \"worked-example\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"No final answer, or steps the learner is meant to supply themselves.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\', \\'spanning\\']\"\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \"projection_hash\": \"05fddc80790c232176df5c03bf7ea1ead8b910d06c848b4836be205a7552c98b\"\\n  },\\n  \"lesson\": {\\n    \"grade_level\": \"Grade 4\",\\n    \"objective\": \"Recognize that plants are producers that make their own food\",\\n    \"subject\": \"Science\"\\n  },\\n  \"sections\": [\\n    {\\n      \"blocks\": [\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Describe a garden where plants grow larger each day. Note that nobody adds food to the garden. Ask students: \\'If no one feeds them, where does the plant\\'s food come from?\\' Use the anchor garden to make the question real.\",\\n          \"id\": \"orient-b1\",\\n          \"intent\": \"orient\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"choices\",\\n            \"figure\",\\n            \"prose\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 0\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Quickly elicit that plants are living things, have parts (roots, stems, leaves), and that all living things need food to grow. Connect this to the garden mystery: plants are growing, so they must get food somehow.\",\\n          \"id\": \"orient-b2\",\\n          \"intent\": \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"choices\",\\n            \"list\",\\n            \"prose\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 1\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"slot_id\": \"orient\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"blocks\": [\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Identify the leaf as the food-making factory. Point to a leaf in the garden example. State that inside the leaf there is a special green substance called chlorophyll that catches light. Mention that water enters through roots and travels up the stem to the leaves, and air (carbon dioxide) enters through tiny pores on the leaf. Do not discuss chloroplasts.\",\\n          \"id\": \"explain-b1\",\\n          \"intent\": \"name-parts\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"figure\",\\n            \"list\",\\n            \"table\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 0\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Explain that chlorophyll uses light energy to combine carbon dioxide from the air and water from the soil into food for the plant. Describe this as photosynthesis: a process that produces food and also releases oxygen. Make clear that the food is made inside the leaf, not taken from the outside. Use the garden plants as the example: \\'The sunshine hits the leaf, the green chlorophyll catches it, and the leaf turns air and water into food.\\' Do not mention glucose or chemical equations.\",\\n          \"id\": \"explain-b2\",\\n          \"intent\": \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"figure\",\\n            \"prose\",\\n            \"table\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 1\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Define \\'producer\\': a living thing that makes its own food. State that plants are producers because they make their own food through photosynthesis. Contrast with animals, which must eat other living things. Reinforce that the garden plants are producers.\",\\n          \"id\": \"explain-b3\",\\n          \"intent\": \"define\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"aside\",\\n            \"prose\",\\n            \"table\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 2\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"slot_id\": \"explain\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"blocks\": [\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Present two identical potted plants from the same garden, same soil, same water. One is placed in a sunny spot; the other is kept in a dark cupboard for two weeks. Describe what students would observe: the sunny plant grows healthy; the dark plant stays small and pale. Ask: \\'Why didn\\'t the dark plant grow even though it had the same soil?\\' Guide students to see that the only difference is light, so light must be necessary for making food. This shows soil is not the food source, because both plants had soil.\",\\n          \"id\": \"contrast-b1\",\\n          \"intent\": \"compare\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"prose\",\\n            \"table\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 0\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Explicitly state: \\'A common mistake is thinking plants eat sunlight. Sunlight is not the food; it\\'s the energy source. The plant uses that energy to build its own food from water and air.\\' This directly counters the \\'plants eat sunlight\\' misconception while reinforcing the previous explanation.\",\\n          \"id\": \"contrast-b2\",\\n          \"intent\": \"warn\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"aside\",\\n            \"prose\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 1\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"slot_id\": \"contrast\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"blocks\": [\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Pose a set of diagnostic questions that require students to apply the core idea. Questions should test: (1) Are plants producers that make their own food? (2) Where in the plant is food made? (3) What captures light? (4) What does a plant need to make food? (5) What happens if light is removed? Use the approved items to form a quiz.\",\\n          \"id\": \"check-b1\",\\n          \"intent\": \"check-understanding\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"choices\",\\n            \"questions\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 0\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"slot_id\": \"check\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}'}], 'model': 'deepseek-v4-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 120000, 'stream': False}}"}
