den where plants grow bigger every day without anyone adding food. Students wonder how they ca\\\\u2026\",\\n      \"id\": \"anchor-1\"\\n    },\\n    \"grade_level\": \"Grade 4\",\\n    \"must_not_introduce\": [\\n      \"chloroplast organelles\",\\n      \"chemical equations of photosynthesis (e.g., 6CO\\\\u2082 + 6H\\\\u2082O \\\\u2192 C\\\\u2086H\\\\u2081\\\\u2082O\\\\u2086 + 6O\\\\u2082)\",\\n      \"glucose as a specific sugar\",\\n      \"light-dependent and light-independent reactions\",\\n      \"limiting factors of photosynthesis\"\\n    ],\\n    \"objective\": \"Recognize that plants are producers that make their own food\",\\n    \"subject\": \"Science\"\\n  },\\n  \"neighbours\": {\\n    \"after\": \"Explicitly state: \\'A common mistake is thinking plants eat sunlight. Sunlight is not the food; it\\'s the energy source. The plant uses that energy to build its own food from water and air.\\' This directly counters the \\'plants eat sunlight\\' misconception while reinforcing the previous explanation.\",\\n    \"before\": \"\"\\n  },\\n  \"section_context\": {\\n    \"section_id\": \"contrast\"\\n  },\\n  \"terminology\": [],\\n  \"writer_contract\": {\\n    \"capacity\": {\\n      \"captionMaxWords\": 20,\\n      \"columnsMax\": 4,\\n      \"columnsMin\": 2,\\n      \"rowsMax\": 8,\\n      \"rowsMin\": 2,\\n      \"wordsPerCell\": 12\\n    },\\n    \"catalogue_version\": \"1.1.0\",\\n    \"content_schema\": {\\n      \"caption\": \"string|null\",\\n      \"columns\": \"TableColumn[]\",\\n      \"presentation\": \"standard|comparison|timeline\",\\n      \"rows\": \"TableRow[]\"\\n    },\\n    \"failure_examples\": [],\\n    \"generation_guidance\": \"\",\\n    \"object_id\": \"table\",\\n    \"object_validation\": []\\n  }\\n}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': \"Return JSON only for this block's content schema.\"}], 'model': 'deepseek-v4-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 120000, 'stream': False}}"}
