{"timestamp": "2026-08-07T17:14:47.151430+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "openai._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-91fab7ae-1e1d-462b-88fe-377f7175b804', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You write one already-planned educational page object.\\n\\nYou may not change:\\n- block ID;\\n- section ID;\\n- position;\\n- pedagogical intent;\\n- requested object type;\\n- lesson objective;\\n- scope restrictions.\\n\\nYour output is the content object only. It must validate against the supplied form schema. Do not wrap it in markdown, explanation, or an object-name envelope.\\n\\nRespect:\\n- grade level;\\n- terminology;\\n- must-not-introduce constraints;\\n- neighboring block summaries;\\n- the specific pedagogical intent;\\n- the block brief.\\n\\nDo not invent answers inside student question content. Assessment answers are returned only through the assessment bundle contract.\\n\\nReturn JSON only for the selected content schema.\\n\\n\\n## INPUT JSON\\n{\\n  \"block\": {\\n    \"brief\": \"Identify the leaf as the food-making factory. Point to a leaf in the garden example. State that inside the leaf there is a special green substance called chlorophyll that catches light. Mention that water enters through roots and travels up the stem to the leaves, and air (carbon dioxide) enters through tiny pores on the leaf. Do not discuss chloroplasts.\",\\n    \"id\": \"explain-b1\",\\n    \"intent\": \"name-parts\",\\n    \"object\": \"figure\",\\n    \"placement\": \"main\",\\n    \"position\": 0\\n  },\\n  \"lesson_context\": {\\n    \"anchor\": {\\n      \"description\": \"A garden where plants grow bigger every day without anyone adding food. Students wonder how they ca\\\\u2026\",\\n      \"id\": \"anchor-1\"\\n    },\\n    \"grade_level\": \"Grade 4\",\\n    \"must_not_introduce\": [\\n      \"chloroplast organelles\",\\n      \"chemical equations of photosynthesis (e.g., 6CO\\\\u2082 + 6H\\\\u2082O \\\\u2192 C\\\\u2086H\\\\u2081\\\\u2082O\\\\u2086 + 6O\\\\u2082)\",\\n      \"glucose as a specific sugar\",\\n      \"light-dependent and light-independent reactions\",\\n      \"limiting factors of photosynthesis\"\\n    ],\\n    \"objective\": \"Recognize that plants are producers that make their own food\",\\n    \"subject\": \"Science\"\\n  },\\n  \"neighbours\": {\\n    \"after\": \"Explain that chlorophyll uses light energy to combine carbon dioxide from the air and water from the soil into food for the plant. Describe this as photosynthesis: a process that produces food and also releases oxygen. Make clear that the food is made inside the leaf, not taken from the outside. Use the garden plants as the example: \\'The sunshine hits the leaf, the green chlorophyll catches it, and the leaf turns air and water into food.\\' Do not mention glucose or chemical equations.\",\\n    \"before\": \"\"\\n  },\\n  \"section_context\": {\\n    \"section_id\": \"explain\"\\n  },\\n  \"terminology\": [],\\n  \"writer_contract\": {\\n    \"capacity\": {\\n      \"altTextMaxWords\": 40,\\n      \"captionMaxWords\": 30\\n    },\\n    \"catalogue_version\": \"1.1.0\",\\n    \"content_schema\": {\\n      \"alt_text\": \"string\",\\n      \"asset\": \"FigureAsset\",\\n      \"caption\": \"string|null\",\\n      \"width\": \"main|span\"\\n    },\\n    \"failure_examples\": [],\\n    \"generation_guidance\": \"\",\\n    \"object_id\": \"figure\",\\n    \"object_validation\": []\\n  }\\n}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': \"Return JSON only for this block's content schema.\"}], 'model': 'deepseek-v4-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 120000, 'stream': False}}"}
