mical equations of photosynthesis (e.g., 6CO\\\\u2082 + 6H\\\\u2082O \\\\u2192 C\\\\u2086H\\\\u2081\\\\u2082O\\\\u2086 + 6O\\\\u2082)\",\\n      \"glucose as a specific sugar\",\\n      \"light-dependent and light-independent reactions\",\\n      \"limiting factors of photosynthesis\"\\n    ],\\n    \"objective\": \"Recognize that plants are producers that make their own food\",\\n    \"subject\": \"Science\"\\n  },\\n  \"neighbours\": {\\n    \"after\": \"\",\\n    \"before\": \"Explain that chlorophyll uses light energy to combine carbon dioxide from the air and water from the soil into food for the plant. Describe this as photosynthesis: a process that produces food and also releases oxygen. Make clear that the food is made inside the leaf, not taken from the outside. Use the garden plants as the example: \\'The sunshine hits the leaf, the green chlorophyll catches it, and the leaf turns air and water into food.\\' Do not mention glucose or chemical equations.\"\\n  },\\n  \"section_context\": {\\n    \"section_id\": \"explain\"\\n  },\\n  \"terminology\": [],\\n  \"writer_contract\": {\\n    \"capacity\": {\\n      \"paragraphsMax\": 4,\\n      \"paragraphsMin\": 1,\\n      \"wordsPerParagraph\": 120\\n    },\\n    \"catalogue_version\": \"1.1.0\",\\n    \"content_schema\": {\\n      \"paragraphs\": \"RichParagraph[]\"\\n    },\\n    \"failure_examples\": [],\\n    \"generation_guidance\": \"\",\\n    \"object_id\": \"prose\",\\n    \"object_validation\": []\\n  }\\n}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': \"Return JSON only for this block's content schema.\"}], 'model': 'deepseek-v4-pro', 'max_completion_tokens': 120000, 'reasoning_effort': 'low', 'stream': False}, 'extra_json': {'thinking': {'type': 'enabled'}}}"}
